A||||2||DreXteR||Front Sway bar... Inner tie rod inspection. == Need Advise==||||7||
Z||000000||DreXteR||02-26-2001||11:43 AM||||I will order these days some parts for my 86 GT. I those parts will be included the sway bars.  Question..  Worth change the stock front sway bar for the one on fiero store??<P>I will order the rear, but Im not sure to order the front one.<P>BTW, how looks a damage inner tie rod?? Inspecting suspension I found the rear rigth have some loose (left to rigth movement).  Take out the wheel, and the outer tie rod looks fine.  Then check the inner tie rod and it looks better!! Almost new(in wear terms). Im confused in here. The inner tie rod is $85.25!  I need to be 300% sure if this one if bad.<P>Thanx.||||reg||7
Z||000001||Oreif||02-26-2001||02:30 PM||||Changing front sway bar to a slightly larger one helps handling. Especially since the new sway bar uses poly bushings.<P>With the tie rods hooked up but the wheel off, What moves? The inner tierod in the rear could have been installed incorrectly and it wore faster. (You stated it looked recent) The inner tie rod should be tight (in and out motion) and stiff up and down.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DreXteR||02-26-2001||11:32 PM||||Problem solved!!  The outer tie rod was losse.<P>Thanx for the help.||||reg||1
